WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.070
- So a Texas church is almost
certainly gonna get sued

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:04.410
for an illegal performance
of the play "Hamilton"

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.810
because they did it without authorization

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:09.004
and added a whole bunch
of anti-gay messaging.

00:00:09.004 --> 00:00:11.430
♪ My hope is in Jesus ♪

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:12.589
- This play is bad.

00:00:12.589 --> 00:00:13.890
♪ No ♪

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.092
- Extremely bad.

00:00:15.092 --> 00:00:17.520
♪ New York ♪
♪ New York ♪

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.217
- And it's almost certainly
copyright infringement.

00:00:19.217 --> 00:00:21.870
But as the original
playwright, Lin-Manuel Miranda,

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.760
said, it's never okay to change the words,

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.040
lyrics, or notes without
their express consent,

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.480
except that sometimes it is.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.090
Sometimes, commentary
and criticism requires

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:32.910
that you change the word
of someone else's IP,

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.110
and these rules can't change

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.790
whether you like the message or not.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.590
In fact, in the seminal case on fair use,

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:40.800
Campbell v. ACUFF-ROSE,
the rap group 2 Live Crew

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.454
changed the words to Roy
Orbison's song "Pretty Woman."

00:00:43.454 --> 00:00:44.370
♪ Big hairy woman ♪

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:46.080
- [Devin] And it was considered parody,

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.834
and it was considered fair use.

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:49.620
♪ You need to shave that stuff ♪

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.270
- Now, that probably doesn't apply here.

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:53.160
This looks like straight-up
copyright infringement.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.930
It doesn't seem like it's a parody.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:56.760
But that being said,
parody doesn't require you

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.710
to agree with the message, and
it's an argument to be made.

